Jacques,

Gerhard Smit here, CTTX in Gqeberha. We engineer owned networks on lodges, re=
serves and farms; we don't sell packages.

You ran Pumba twice as GM, so you know the gaps better than I do: between Wat=
er Lodge and Msenge, out to the rangers and the gates, and after hours. Pumba=
 has said publicly that a rhino incident runs about seven minutes from dartin=
g to departure. A response inside that window depends on the network reaching=
 the field, not only the lodges.

We've done a desktop terrain study of Pumba from 30 m satellite elevation dat=
a and cloud-free imagery. It's attached, one page, no pricing. What it found:

- Two ridge high sites on the reserve, one at about 690 m in the north and on=
e at about 510 m in the south, 6.1 km apart with a clear path between them.
- Both lodges sit on clear radio paths from the southern site: Water Lodge at=
 3.0 km and Msenge at 4.4 km, each with well over the 60% Fresnel clearance w=
e design to.
- A candidate carrier uplink of 14.2 km from the Makhanda high ground into th=
e southern site.
- About 87% of the 60 km2 study area is in line of sight of those two sites, =
which is where cameras, gates and ranger radios would live.

Those positions are desktop candidates until we walk them. What the study say=
s is that Pumba can own one backbone that carries the lodges, the security op=
eration and the payments behind them, instead of renting lodge Wi-Fi on separ=
ate lines and leaving the field dark.

The next step is a half-day assessment on site: what you have, what fails, wh=
at it costs you, and what an owned network would look like, with the high sit=
es and the uplink confirmed on the ground. R3,500 ex VAT, credited against th=
e build, and the report is yours either way. If you share the lodges' current=
 connectivity invoices, I'll put Pumba's actual payback in that report.

Can I call you for 10 minutes this week?

Gerhard Smit
Director | CTTX Services (Pty) Ltd
gerhard@cttx.co.za | 041 371 1089 | 084 550 3281
www.cttx.co.za

If this isn't relevant to you, reply "no thanks" and I won't follow up.

